# React components

Use functional components. Split **smart** (container) and **dumb** (presentational).

## Placement

- **Smart:** `src/screens/*Screen.tsx` — data, routing, hooks, services. Compose views; keep JSX thin.
- **Dumb:** `src/screens/components/*`, `*View.tsx` — render props, emit callbacks. No fetch, Dexie, routers, or domain services.
- Shared UI pieces live in `screens/components/`. Do not nest new presentational components inside a Screen file.

## Rules

- Screens default-export the page. Reusable UI uses named exports.
- Type props with `FooProps`. Prefer `function Foo({ ... }: FooProps)` over `FC`.
- Dumb components receive data + `onEvent` callbacks. They may hold **local UI state** (input text, open/closed) but not app/session state.
- Do not put learning/FSRS/DB logic in components. Call hooks or `src/services/`.
- Do not export helpers from Screen files. Put them in `src/utils/` or a hook.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — Screen fetches and paints details
export default function WordDetailScreen() {
  const [word, setWord] = useState<Word | null>(null);
  useEffect(() => { db.words.get(id).then(setWord); }, [id]);
  return <div>{word?.lemma}</div>;
}

// ✅ GOOD — Screen wires; View renders
export default function WordDetailScreen() {
  const { word, onBack } = useWordDetail();
  return <WordDetailView word={word} onBack={onBack} />;
}

export function WordDetailView({ word, onBack }: WordDetailViewProps) {
  return <section><BackButton onClick={onBack} /><h1>{word.lemma}</h1></section>;
}
```
